---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import LobsterFriend from '../assets/lobster-friend.png';
---

<PageLayout
	title="About"
	description="About The Sophomore."
>
	<section class="content-shell py-12 space-y-8"> 
		<div class="space-y-4 max-w-3xl">
			<h1 class="m-0 text-ink text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight">About</h1>
			<p class="m-0 text-muted text-lg">
 <em>The Sophomore <em> was founded in 2024 as space to pursue independent thinking. At its core it is a platform for the continued production of thought outside of a strictly academic environment. As it exists now,  <em>The Sophomore <em> publishes materials online on culture, criticism, technology, history, and more. These categories are not intended to be exhaustive nor a limit to what will be published online. 
			</p>
			<p class="m-0 mt-6 text-ink text-2xl font-semibold">Mission statement </p>
			<p class="m-0 text-muted text-lg">
The etymology of “sophomore”—combining the Greek words  <em>sophistēs<em>, meaning wisdom, and  <em>mōros<em>, meaning foolish, describes a wise fool. It describes the transition from being foolish to wanting to be wise. It reflects a thirst for knowledge while being open to engagement, an openness to be corrected, and an openness to appear foolish in order to become wise. Afterall, we are all still only sophomores.
			</p>

			<Image
				src={LobsterFriend}
				alt="Lobster"
				width={512}
				class="mt-8 w-48 h-auto"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
